# Functions & Queries

Every function and every database query gets **one short comment** above it — a few words only. No long paragraphs.

## Comments

- Say what it does in plain words, like explaining to a friend.
- **3–8 words** is enough. One line max.
- Comment every function and every SQL/query block — not every single line inside.

```javascript
// ❌ BAD — too long
// This function takes the donor id from the request, validates all required fields,
// checks if the user is verified, then inserts a new donation record into MongoDB
// and returns the created document with a 201 status code.

// ✅ GOOD
// Add a new food donation
async function createDonation(req, res) { ... }

// ✅ GOOD
// Get available food near a city
function getNearbyDonations(city) { ... }
```

```sql
-- ❌ BAD
-- Retrieves all donation records from the donations table where status is available
-- and the best_before timestamp is greater than the current time, ordered by date

-- ✅ GOOD
-- List food still available
SELECT * FROM donations WHERE status = 'available' AND best_before > NOW();
```

## One Thing Per Function

- Each function does **one job only**. If it does two jobs, split it.
- Name the function after that one job: `validateDonation`, `saveDonation`, `sendClaimAlert`.
- Don't mix validation + save + email in one function.

```javascript
// ❌ BAD — does too much in one place
async function handleDonation(req, res) {
  // validate, save, notify NGOs, update stats, send email...
}

// ✅ GOOD — split into small pieces
// Check donation form fields
function validateDonation(data) { ... }

// Save donation to database
async function saveDonation(data) { ... }

// Notify nearby NGOs
async function notifyNearbyNGOs(donation) { ... }
```

## Queries

- One query = one purpose. Don't cram unrelated reads/writes into one query.
- If you need join + filter + sort for one screen, that's fine — it's still one job (e.g. "get donor dashboard listings").
